[h1]GK2 HUD+[/h1]
Quality-of-life features for Graveyard Keeper 2 in one mod. More numbers, more context, a better map and a calendar. It looks like the game made it.

[b]Looks native.[/b] Built from the game's own UI: same fonts, frames, colors and pixel grid.
[b]No spoilers.[/b] It only shows what your save has already revealed.
[b]Information first.[/b] Nothing changes the rules by default. The two features that do ship turned off.
[b]Toggles live.[/b] Every feature turns on and off from the [b]GK2 HUD+[/b] button in the pause menu, without restarting.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Map[/b]: mouse wheel zoom, look inside places you have visited, item details on the town orders icon.
[*][b]Tooltips[/b]: hovering shows the essentials; middle click pins the tooltip and opens the details (recipe in item cells, where it is used, costs per tick). Highlighted terms open another tooltip inside it.
[*][b]Tooltips in the world[/b]: rest the mouse on a craft, a garden bed or a body to see what is being made, the progress cells and how long is left.
[*][b]Calendar[/b]: time and week on the day medallion, a calendar tab and a journal of what you unlocked each day.
[*][b]Quest tree[/b]: NPC names, and click a quest to read how you got there.
[*][b]HUD[/b]: numbers on the energy and insanity bars, optional day and time plate, turning medallion.
[*][b]Optional, off by default[/b]: Save and Load in the pause menu, zombie perk refund.
[/list]

The key that pins a tooltip can be changed in the game's Controls window (last line of the list).

[h2]Install[/h2]
Subscribe. The game installs and updates the mod by itself; it starts on the next launch.

This is a [b]BepInEx plugin[/b]. Steam Deck and Linux (Proton): set the game's launch options to
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winhttp=n,b" %command%[/code]

English and Brazilian Portuguese, following the game's language.

[h2]Source[/h2]
Clips of every feature, source code and releases: [url=https://github.com/MullerVGS/gk2-hud-plus]github.com/MullerVGS/gk2-hud-plus[/url]
